+  `:selenium` into `:cuprite` (`browser_options: { "no-sandbox" => nil }`), then requires
+  `application_system_test_case`. Run one test per process (`-n /name/`) to tell the sign-in flake
+  below apart from real failures.
+- Small containers: `bin/rails server` in development forks one Puma worker per CPU. Set
+  `WEB_CONCURRENCY=1` or Chromium may get OOM-killed.
+- Under cuprite, the multi-session tests (`sending_messages_test.rb`, `boosting_messages_test.rb`)
+  are flaky (`ObsoleteNode`, failed `sign_in`), on a pristine checkout too. Rerun them on their own
+  before suspecting a change. `sign_in` itself (`system_test_helper.rb:9`, "found `<<ERROR>>`")
+  also fails intermittently in single-session tests, untouched ones like `unread_rooms_test.rb`
+  included; a failure *there* is never about the test body.
